	(text "19.2 MHz crystal (FSLC[2:0] = 000)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 280.7303 146.77 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0229b2d4-1dcd-5be5-9dbb-929a3e9f9fc5")
	)
	(text "12 pF load: C1 = C2 = 2 x (12 pF - ~5 pF stray) = 14 pF -> 12 pF.  No series resistor; within 2 cm, no vias (AN70707 s.5).\nDrive level 0.14 mW at most (AN70707 eq. 1: C0 3 pF, ESR 50 ohm, YXC's maxima): within YXC's 0.2 mW rating."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 280.7303 152.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "05d199b4-232d-5ba8-b776-3ad1ac803725")
	)
	(text "On the FX3's SPI balls, which carry its UART in 32-bit GPIF mode: SSN is held high so a fitted flash stays deselected then.\nIt can hold the FX3 firmware (SPI boot) and the FPGA image.  The 2k MISO pull-down is for SPI boot (AN70707 s.8.5)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8125 274.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "13ed6632-78af-56fb-926d-9136cd897c2b")
	)
	(text "FX3 debug connectors: JTAG (Tag-Connect TC2050, ARM 10-pin order) and UART (3-pin, 2.54 mm, not fitted), both 3.3 V"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 337.0815 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "2859dff7-7da9-51d9-956e-cb9e5cdfdc78")
	)
	(text "Optional SPI flash for standalone boot (not fitted)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 177.8125 268.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "45b68843-07b2-55ab-9132-516ad44c72ac")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups to VIO5 (3.3 V), as the FX3 requires."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 338.212 271.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "6a415b57-41a6-57a7-a8be-89173837561b")
	)
	(text "3  USB 3 controller: Infineon EZ-USB FX3 (CYUSB3014-BZXI)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "92771dcb-f6b8-52a1-9161-46f00b6d9cfb")
	)
	(text "FX3 supply filtering and decoupling (AN70707 table 3, figure 1, figure 6)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 146.77 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "96c5daee-5646-5571-b42e-5eb6e6a96ed4")
	)
	(text "AVDD and CVDDQ through 600 ohm beads, U3TXVDDQ and U3RXVDDQ through 120 ohm ones (0.05 ohm DC); VDD without a bead.\n2 x 47 uF on VDD and 2 x 100 uF on each USB 3 rail supply the PHY's start-up inrush (up to 0.8 A for 10 us): on each USB 3\nrail one 100 uF (0805) sits beside its 100 nF at the FX3's edge, on short, wide copper to the ball, and the other (1206) at\nits bead.  At the regulator's +/-1 % corners VDD stays within 1.176 ... 1.236 V and the USB 3 rails at 1.157 V or above at\ntheir balls (simulated with the copper as laid out; with AN70707's 600 ohm beads and 2 x 47 uF they dipped to 1.10 V)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 159.17 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a65e594b-4846-5bac-913c-04211586f05b")
	)
	(text "JTAG for firmware debug with a J-Link or other ARM9 probe (no SWD on the FX3): TC2050-IDC cable, TC2050-ARM2010 adapter.  TDI,\nTMS, TRST# have internal 50k pull-ups, TCK a 10k pull-down (AN70707 s.8.2).  Pin 9 is ground (ARM's layout: keep the adapter's\nnTRST bridge open), TRST# has its own pad; ~RESET (10) pulls RESET# low.  UART: 1 GND, 2 FX3 RX (in), 3 FX3 TX (out), 3.3 V only.\nRecovery with a fitted flash: short UART pins 3 and 1 (MISO to ground) during power-up, so the boot ROM reads no valid image\nand falls back to USB boot (not tested)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 349.4815 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "ae38513e-4b92-58b1-9ec9-32806b659b2c")
	)
	(text "PMODE[2:0] = Z11: USB boot; the host loads the firmware at each connection.  Standalone boot from the optional flash below:\nfit the PMODE2 pull-down and remove the PMODE1 pull-up (0Z1 = SPI, falling back to USB).\nRESET# follows VBUS (10k / 15k, 1 uF: 6 ms): when the Pi powers the board before a USB cable is plugged in, the FX3 stays in\nreset until VBUS arrives, as its USB boot requires (datasheet errata 2).  3.30 V at VBUS 5.5 V, under the pin's CVDDQ + 0.3 V\nlimit; 2.46 V at 4.1 V (where the FX3 sees VBUS), above VIH = 0.625 x CVDDQ."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 280.7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b5317ab7-1511-506e-a4a3-8d22723d626f")
	)
	(text "Boot mode, reset"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 268.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b60df71a-32c5-502c-885f-15876533123b")
	)
	(text "GPIF II, 32-bit slave FIFO to the FPGA (DQ[0..31], PCLK driven by the FPGA, CTL[0..8], CTL[11..12]).  32-bit mode costs the SPI\nport; UART, I2S and I2C remain.  The FPGA is configured in slave serial: CCLK = I2S_CLK, DIN = I2S_SD (I2S DMA or GPIO), PROGRAM_B =\nCTL9, DONE = CTL10, INIT_B = GPIO45.  I2C (400 kHz) is the register bus to the FPGA.  VIO1-3 = 1.8 V (interface to the FPGA),\nVIO4 / VIO5 / CVDDQ = 3.3 V.  VBATT open: the USB 2.0 PHY runs from VBUS (as on CYUSB3KIT-003).  The GPIF lines have no series\nresistors: both ends are within 3 cm; set both to low drive strength (a strong 20 ohm driver overshoots 0.4 ... 0.7 V in\nsimulation, a 40 ohm one 0.13 V at most).  Check with IBIS models at layout (AN70707 s.6).\nCLKIN / CLKIN_32, OTG_ID, INT#, I2S_WS / MCLK, O[60] (D11) and NC (A11) are open."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 42 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d341701c-10b8-553f-93ab-d9d776f811e9")
	)
	(text "U: CYUSB3014-BZXI (Infineon datasheet 001-52136 rev *Z; hardware rules from AN70707 rev *Q)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 25.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "eeb9b649-0a1a-5fac-9f29-2693f57e3283")
	)
